A||||15||mshill||Best Dash Speaker replacements...||||1||
Z||000000||mshill||09-06-2001||01:44 AM||||I am helping my son restore his Fiero and was looking at Crutchfields and they show only two choices for the 4x10s: Pioneer T-A4103 and the Kenwood KFC-415C.  They are both priced at $99.95/pair.  Which is better and is there a cheaper alternative that would have similar qualities when mated to a 52W (max) per channel head unit?||||reg||1
Z||000001||MontanaFiero||09-06-2001||02:13 AM||||Look at the Kenwoods.. the old style (last year's model) had a thick plastic spacer that made them too thick to mount in the dash because you couldn't put the cover back on.--- the new ones (I believe) don't have this problem. I like kenwood, and if you can, that's what I would do.<P>Suggest going to a store and actually looking at them.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||09-06-2001||02:21 AM||||I've replaced several with the Pioneers and have had no problems.<P>My $.02||||reg||1
Z||000003||RossT||09-06-2001||02:24 AM||||I have that kenwood model.  No problems with instalation.  But you can buy them cheaper at:<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.onlinecarstereo.com" TARGET=_blank>www.onlinecarstereo.com</A> <P>But I did buy the speaker wire harness from<BR>crutchfield for 5 bucks.  It makes instalation much easier.<P>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 09-06-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Kasdan||09-06-2001||07:01 AM||||When i got my car, it had those exactl pioneers in it.  They were all brittle and cracked, go with the Kenwood.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||09-06-2001||12:15 PM||||I have no recommendations on the factory size.<P>If your looking for a little bit more work, 6x9's can be massaged in. I've got a pair of 6x9 Boston Accoustics in mine and love them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||09-06-2001||12:34 PM||||i'm using 2 pairs of MB Quart 4" coaxial. the plate took about 20minutes to make.. 1/4" fiber board and a jig saw. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||09-06-2001||01:03 PM||||I would recommend going to 4" components also.  4x10s, well, they kinda suck.  Like Trav said, the mounting plate is very easy to make.  I think Crutchfield might actually already have one, might be worth looking in to.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Joe Torma||09-06-2001||01:09 PM||||The only thing I have against the 4's is that you lose some midbass.  Whatever you pu in there, make sure is has some sort of enclosure under it.  Lots of speakers don't sound right free-air.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haagster||09-06-2001||02:40 PM||||I've got Kicker 4x10 speakers in my dash.  They sound decent, although I couldn't win any competition with them...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_4.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000010||FieroPerformance||09-06-2001||02:59 PM||||I have the pioneer speakers in my car, I bought them at best buy for $80. They sound awesome! (I have a blaupunkt casablanca cd50 head unit so that is probably part of it). Anyway, they sound great, they can't handle bass very well though, I suggest a sub or 6x9 speakers.<P>-Charlie<p>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Bruce||09-06-2001||04:01 PM||||If you want a REALLY cheap replacement, I have a pair of stock 4x10's that I replaced when I redid the speaker grill fabric. There are in great shape and I think they sound pretty good. The price is right (free); just let me know if you want them.<BR>bb||||reg||1
Z||000012||Joe Torma||09-06-2001||04:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroPerformance:<BR><B>I have the pioneer speakers in my car, I bought them at best buy for $80. ...Anyway, they sound great, they can't handle bass very well though, I suggest a sub or 6x9 speakers.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You need an enclosure to get good bass....go to a fabric shop and buy 1/2" foam and lay it in the speaker hole and screw the speaker on top...that should help a bit.  Or look in Crutchfield for preformed foam enclosures<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||JohnF||09-06-2001||05:59 PM||||With my crossed fingers, Pioneers are still going strong hooked up to my Blaupunkt w/CD.  Hard to beat for the price!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Spektrum-87GT||09-06-2001||09:53 PM||||i have a pioneer head unit(deh-2100) and i love it, cheap and a great cd player, NEVER skips. I do have one problem with it... the plastic is so cheap! the detachable face feels like its going to break every time i take off!<P>my bad, thought you were talking about cd players, good info none the less!<p>[This message has been edited by Spektrum-87GT (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Monkeyman||09-07-2001||05:35 AM||||A lot of this depends on how much you're willing to pay for what quality sound.  I scrapped my dash speakers all together and bought some of AusFieros door speaker pods and some Kenwood 5 1/4" components.  They sound a million times better than any stock speakers I've had.  I also bought Aus' center console sub box and added a Cerwin Vega 10" sub.  All of this mated to a Kenwood amp and a Sony head unit.  I think it sounds awesome (although not competition quality--that's not what I was after).<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
